A||N||12||Monkeyman||WHERE DO I DRILL????||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||03-22-2000||09:33 PM||||I only have a couple of days left before it starts to rain again.  I need to know where to drill the drain holes for my sunroof.  It leaks bad!!!  I'm ruining what's left of my seats.  This is in the Grape Ape ('85 GT).||||reg||5
Z||000001||mutfish||03-22-2000||10:23 PM||||how about the floor........||||reg||1
Z||000002||Earne||03-23-2000||07:32 AM||||Monkeyman, how 'bout a brand spankin' new OEM sunroof weatherstrip?  Give me your address and $25 and it's yours.  Bought as a "just in case," won't need, goin' with new tops.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BOILERMAKER||03-23-2000||07:35 AM||||You may want to think about caulking it up for the "quick fix" to get you through the rain.<P>I believe there are a few drain holes, but I can't remember right now where they are without going out to the car to check.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||03-23-2000||09:33 AM||||You drill into the front corners. The best way to see the exact spots is to go to a junkyard and find a Fiero (87 or 88) with a sunroof and lift the seal out of the corners and you will see the drain holes. I can't be more exact because I did mine 4 years ago when I changed out the seal.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||03-23-2000||01:13 PM||||Also don't forget to check the gaskets for the bolts that go through the glass! I had a real bad problem with this and noticed that the gaskets that attach the release mechanism were cracked. I didn't have any gaskets so I used tiny o-rings for a quick fix. I noticed a drop in water levels but not complete. I than got some gasket material and replaced them myself. Fixed!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||03-23-2000||05:59 PM||||Earne--Out of $$ at the moment, but if you still have the seal/weatherstrip in a couple of weeks, it's mine!<P>Oreif--I figured it was the front corners, but there aren't any '87 or '88s around that I can get access to.  Would the '86s have the same holes?  The Monkeymobile never leaked ('86 SC) but I don't want to tear up the seal for no reason.<P>WKDFIRO--I used the sunroof panel out of the Monkeymobile.  I just replaced the "hinges" and the plastic washers.  Thanx, though.<P>Are there any special drain tubes in the cars that had the drain holes drilled from the factory?  I'd hate to drill holes just to get the water to drip on my feet instead of my head!||||reg||1
Z||000007||ROB MAC||03-23-2000||07:04 PM||||Before you spend cash did you remove the window, clean it and the rubber real good (all that crud made mine leak every spring) then put it back on just right? I got sick of sniffin engine fumes and sealed mine with silicone. Can't say I miss being able to open it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||03-23-2000||07:17 PM||||MM.<P>I'd seriously consider droping the headliner to better see where it's leaking. It it's getting between the seal and glass I don't think the drains will help much. You shouldn't need the whole headliner out. just the trim around the roof glass should let you see better.<P>Are you sure you have the glass latch adjusted right? If it's too loose or too tight it can cause leaks.<P>The way I do these type latches......<P>take off the trim. (one phylips screw) then lossen the 2 nuts and close the latch.<P>Hold the latch plate in place carefully and release the latch. slide the latch to the rear just a tiny bit. about 1/64-1/32 of an inch is all you want. tighten the nuts.<P>Give it a leak test. If that doesn't get it try doing the same but sliding forward the same amount.<P>It sounds dumb but the latch plate position is important. The position is what fine tunes the tightness of the whole roof glass.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TOM||03-23-2000||08:48 PM||||The drain holes let the water run off even if the seal does leak. It drains before it has a chance to get high enough to fill the chanel and run into the car. No tubes. Just the holes.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||03-24-2000||08:31 AM||||Headliner's already out (using the one from the Monkeymobile so I can have a 3rd brake light).  It's filling up the trough then leaking into the car.  I'm using the sunroof glass from the Monkeymobile which has new hinges, etc. so I know that's not it.  The weatherstrip is iffy so I'm getting a new one just to be sure.  I'll try drilling the holes today (supposed to rain tonight).  We'll see in the morning if that works.  If not, I'll try adjusting the hinge although it's still in the factory position.<P>Thanx, guys! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||03-24-2000||08:49 AM||||MM,<P>The latch plate I'm talking about isn't on the glass. It's the bracket that the roof anchors to in the rear. If it's out of whack then it can cause a leak. I'd at least take the trim off the bracket and make sure it's tight. It can feel tighter in use than it really is. ((I was amazed how loose the nuts on my bracket where when I adjusted it a couple weeks ago.))||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||03-24-2000||10:42 AM||||I just drilled a hole in each corner.  I'll check the bracket this afternoon.  Like I said, it appears to be in the factory position, but I'm sure it could have moved some over the years.  I didn't know that as little as 1/64th of an inch could make a difference.  It wouldn't surprise me if it move 3 or 4 times that much.  ||||reg||1
